With numpy:
```
import numpy as np
lc_arr = np.array(lc)  # size k
cur_arr = np.array(cur)  # size k, updated as we sweep
for c in csorted_desc:
    # advance pos to fc[c], updating cur_arr
    rolled = np.roll(lc_arr, -c)  # rolled[a] = lc[(a+c)%k]
    mask = cur_arr <= (rolled - 1)
    if mask.any():
        v = (rolled - fc[c])[mask].max()
        best = max(best, v)
```
